# Terraform working files. None of these belongs in version control, and two of
# them would be an outright disclosure: terraform.tfvars is where
# account-specific values go, and terraform.tfstate records every attribute of
# every resource, including account numbers and full ARNs.
.terraform/
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Everything except the committed example.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Saved plans. A plan file contains the same values the state does.
*.tfplan

# .terraform.lock.hcl is NOT ignored. It pins provider versions by checksum and
# belongs in version control. It is absent at the time this configuration was
# written because the session that wrote it had no route to
# registry.terraform.io, so no provider could be resolved to lock. The runbook
# asks the operator to generate it for every platform the project is applied
# from and commit it:
#
#   terraform providers lock \
#     -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64 -platform=darwin_amd64
